    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (73.12) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.07) serving as our primary offensive engines. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a massive SP advantage against Kendry Rojas (5.83 xERA), and despite the platoon disadvantage, his elite xwOBA remains the cornerstone of our daily floor. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is an aggressive play today; his score is buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and favorable wind conditions, which override the risk of facing a pitcher like Brandon Sproat who limits stolen base opportunities. **Trea Turner** (71.38) remains a locked-in must-start, as his leadoff spot and favorable wind/park factor compensate for a moderate matchup against the left-handed Nick Lodolo.\n\nConversely, we are closely monitoring the bottom of the lineup and our bench decisions. **Colt Keith** (68.01) is the standout of our mid-tier, maximizing his value through a prime leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Cecconi. The most difficult bench decision involved **Hyeseong Kim** (47.43), who sat just outside the starting rotation. While **Hyeseong Kim** carries a strong platoon edge, the optimizer favored **Luke Raley** (48.62) and **Dillon Dingler** (48.56) due to the higher variance potential for counting stats in their respective lineup slots. We are particularly concerned about **Christian Yelich** (54.29) and **Gary Sanchez** (57.30), both of whom face Shota Imanaga; the wind blowing out at the park provides a slight cushion, but their efficiency scores are hampered by the lefty-lefty matchup and Imanaga\u2019s solid baseline metrics.\n\nOperational risk remains elevated as several names, including **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Luke Raley**, and **Junior Caminero**, are pending official lineup confirmation. While we have projected their batting order, any mid-day shifts\u2014especially for **Caleb Durbin** or **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2014could necessitate a roster pivot to protect our daily game caps. We have confirmed that **Zac Veen** remains unavailable due to his status with the Albuquerque Isotopes, and **Kyle Schwarber** is excluded from the active rotation today. Maintain close watch on the weather and official batting orders for the latest updates.",
